> >> > > > Below is the patch against to Kernel 4.8 & 4.9. Please review.
> >> > > >
> >> > > > I checked the drivers/pci/quirks.c, it looks the=20
> >> > > > workarounds/fixes in quirks.c are for specific devices and=20
> >> > > > one or more device ID are defined for the specific devices.=20
> >> > > > However my patch is for all AMD SR-IOV capable GPUs, that includ=
es all existing and future AMD server GPUs.
> >> > > > So it doesn't seem like a good fit to put the fix in quirks.c. =
=20
> >> > >
> >> > >
> >> > > Why is an AMD graphics card unique here?  Doesn't sriov_init()=20
> >> > > always need to be able to deal with devices of any type where=20
> >> > > the BIOS hasn't initialized the SR-IOV capability?  Some SR-IOV=20
> >> > > devices can fit their VFs within a minimum bridge aperture,=20
> >> > > most cannot.  I don't understand why the VF resource=20
